    "John Barnard Jenkins was born in Cardiff on 11 March 1933 and grew up at Penybryn, near Gelligaer, where the family moved during the Second World War. He passed the eleven-plus for Bargoed Grammar School, but left at thirteen to be apprenticed to a blacksmith, and later worked at the Lysaght steelworks in Newport. In 1950 he joined the army. He served in Berlin, Germany and Cyprus, and rose to be a sergeant in the Royal Army Dental Corps. (Source: Wyn Thomas, John Jenkins: The Reluctant Revolutionary?, Y Lolfa, 2019.)",
